fact WorkItem(id: "WI-304", description: some(value: "Build the operation-body NodeOccurrence natively in convert_expr_term (parse IR to occurrence), eliminating the materialize_from_handle round-trip at the op-body load site (load.rs:5828-5829). Op-body analog of WI-246 (rule bodies); finishes WI-251 item (e) (eliminate the double tree walk by building NodeOccurrence trees directly in convert_expr_term), which was left undone when WI-251 was delivered. TODAY: loader does convert_expr_term (parse to reflect-form Term handle) then materialize_from_handle (Term to occurrence via visit_fn last-segment name-matching re-inference). The handle is vestigial as a term: nobody reads OperationInfo.body / OperationImpl.body as a term; all consumers (cpp-gen OpImplTable WI-249, typer WI-247, eval WI-248, req_insertion, op_requirements, op_info, simp_rewrite) read the occurrence via kb.op_body_node / op_bodies. PLAN: thread a parallel occ_results Vec<Rc<NodeOccurrence>> through convert_expr_terms work-stack walker (visit_load / build_load). Leaves build their Expr leaf directly (Const/VarRef/Var/Ref/Ident), NOT via materialize_from_handle. Internal frames assemble the Expr variant from child occurrences; the pure assembly helper node_occurrence::build_frame can be reused since it touches no KB terms. let/lambda/match keep pattern/param as a TermId field from the term side (Expr::Let.pattern is a TermId), so the pattern childs occurrence is discarded, not consumed: mind the stack discipline (term results and occ_results diverge on patterns). Guards are always none in convert today (build_load sets guard=build_none). Use the natively-built occurrence at the op-body site instead of materialize_from_handle; set_op_body_node(functor, native_occ). Keep building the term handle for the OperationInfo.body field until WI-252 retires it. SCOPE: op-body load path only. materialize_from_handle STAYS for its other callers (rule-body reflect-form atoms at build_body_atom_occurrence:4662; the apply_subst+materialize reflection/typer-rewriter reify path at node_occurrence.rs:1286); deleting it entirely plus dropping the handle is gated on WI-252 (drop OperationInfo.body field, migrate the OperationInfo(body: some) presence check to op_body_node) and migrating those remaining callers natively. ACCEPTANCE: op-body occurrence built without any materialize_from_handle call; cargo test green (typer + cpp-gen + eval exercise op bodies); native occurrence matches prior materialize output as verified by the suite."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-24T15:44:36Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-304", author: "user", content: "Delivered commit 26e7dc7. convert_expr_term now returns (TermId, Rc<NodeOccurrence>) and builds the op-body occurrence natively via a parallel expr_occ_results stack: leaves through node_occurrence::build_expr_leaf, internal frames reuse build_frame (pub(crate)), let/lambda/match patterns occ-suppressed (PushOccSuppress/PopOccSuppress), match branches via an expr_match_metas side stack. Op-body site no longer calls materialize_from_handle; term handle still built for OperationInfo.body (WI-252 to retire it). materialize_from_handle retained for rule-body reflect atoms + the apply_subst reify path. Behavior-preserving (more precise spans); full workspace 1237 green incl. 2 new wi304 tests; multi-agent code-review found no active bugs.", at: "2026-05-24T15:44:36Z")
